  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 1.2. Increased institutional capacity of workers&#x2019; organizations</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Federation of Trade Unions of Ukraine (FPU) and the Confederation of Free Trade Unions of Ukraine (KVPU) developed a joint trade union position paper on labour law reform in February 2022. Compliance with International Labour Standards was highlighted in the paper.

Labour law reforms in Ukraine are, according to the trade unions, continuing to undermine workers&apos; rights in the country. The draft Law No. 5371 (on the contractual regime for the regulation of employment relations) was adopted on 19 July 2022 and signed by the President on 17th of August. Under the law, two thirds of employees in Ukraine will lose the protection they had under previous laws. It will make it harder for trade unions to remain relevant and provide services to workers in small and medium sized enterprises.


 The ILO provide support to the process of drafting the trade union position paper on labour law reform with contribution of the Government of Denmark through the project Inclusive labour markets for job creation in Ukraine (UKR/17/01/DNK). The position paper was guided by the joint UN position paper on labour law reform, developed with ILO support in 2020.</narrative>
   </description>
